Attribution and provenance notice
==================================

JSGA is a from-scratch Java re-implementation, informed by and functionally
modeled on the algorithms and behavior of GAucsd 1.4 (1993), a C genetic
algorithm toolkit originally developed as GENESIS by John J. Grefenstette
(Navy Center for Applied Research in Artificial Intelligence) and later
extended and maintained as "GAucsd" by Nicol N. Schraudolph at the University
of California, San Diego. No original GAucsd/GENESIS source code is
redistributed as part of this repository; this project independently
implements equivalent behavior in Java. See the README for a package-by-
package mapping between GAucsd's C modules and JSGA's Java classes.

The original GAucsd distribution (available at
https://nic.schraudolph.org/pubs/GAucsd.sh.gz) does not include a formal
open-source license (e.g., an SPDX-identified license) in its README or
source files; it was distributed for free academic and research use. Anyone
wishing to use, redistribute, or build upon the original GAucsd/GENESIS C
source directly (as opposed to this independent Java implementation) should
contact the original authors or consult UC San Diego's records for the
applicable terms.
